Replies interleave answers beneath the quoted lines, so a question or
request for the reader can sit anywhere in a long mail and be missed.
Pat then has to read the whole reply to learn where the work stands
and what he must do next.

A fixed summary at the end answers that in one place. Its objective is
the thread's end goal, because the step a reply just finished says
nothing about how far the work is from landing. Done is reserved for a
reached goal with nothing left for the reader; calling work done while
asking the reader to test or review it hides that it still waits on
him. A reply that is not done and asks for nothing shows that the work
stopped without reason.
