+## End each reply with status and asks
+
+Questions and requests scattered through an interleaved reply are easy
+to miss. End every reply that is not a patch with a short summary, so
+the reader sees at a glance where the work stands and what is asked of
+them:
+
+    Objective: <the end goal of the thread>
+    Status: <done, or what it is waiting on>
+    Next actions for you:
+    - <what the reader must do, or "none">
+    Information needed from you:
+    - <what you need to know, or "none">
+
+The objective is the outcome the thread exists to reach, such as a
+port accepted into the tree. It is not the step this reply finished,
+such as answering a question or posting a revision. Name the same
+objective in every reply on the thread until it is reached.
+
+Done and a next action for the reader exclude each other. The status
+is done only when the objective is reached and nothing is left for the
+reader. While the reader still has to review, test, or decide, the
+objective is not done; the status names what it waits on, and the two
+lists say what the reader must do or provide. A status that is not
+done, with "none" in both lists, means you stopped without cause.
+Finish the work instead.
+
+Interleaved answers stay where they are. The summary repeats any ask
+made above it, so the reader can act on the summary alone.
+
 ## Read the whole batch before working
 
